Rule 1 (input must be a tensor, not a dtype object; suppresses torch.dtype AttributeError)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 2 (all dimensions are valid non-negative sizes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0 ∧ shape(v_1, i) ≤ 2147483647)
>>
Rule 3 (for non-empty tensors, min is not greater than max)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) then min(v_1) ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (valid dtype object associated with the tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (valid last-axis indexing if tensor is not scalar)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 0) ∨ (shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) ≥ 0)
